Junit-
-------
- Java testing framework -> helps to write and run unit tests
- types of testing with Junit
	- isolation testing
	- integration testing


Junit Testing(Isolation)
-------------------------
Characteristics
- Tests only one class or method.
- Dependencies (database, APIs, services) are mocked or stubbed.
- Fast execution.
- Easy to identify bugs.

class Calculator {
    int add(int a, int b) {
        return a + b;
    }
}

public class CalculatorTest {
    @Test
    void testAddition() {
        Calculator calculator = new Calculator();
        assertEquals(5, calculator.add(2, 3));
    }
}

Mock objects - dummy data -> Mockito
-------------
Mock objects are used in JUnit isolation (unit) testing to replace real dependencies, allowing a class
or method to be tested independently without interacting with external systems.

Constructor Based Dependency Injection vs @Autowired
-----------------------------------------------------
Constructor-based injection passes dependencies through the constructor, making them explicit, immutable, and easy to mock in JUnit tests.

Field injection using @Autowired injects dependencies directly into fields, which hides dependencies and makes unit testing more difficult. Therefore, constructor-based injection is the preferred approach in Spring applications.


Junit Testing(Integration)
-----------------------------
Characteristics
- Tests interactions between multiple classes/modules.
- Uses real or test databases, APIs, or external services.
- Slower than unit tests.
- Validates complete workflows.

@SpringBootTest
public class UserServiceIntegrationTest {
    @Autowired
    private UserService userService;

    @Test
    void testCreateUser() {
        User user = userService.createUser("John");
        assertNotNull(user.getId());
    }
}


JaCoCo
-----------
- how much of your code was actually executed when you ran your tests.
- works as plugin with Junit
- often required for CI/CD quality gates(e.g.,"Fail build if coverage <80%").



Note: we should perform -ve and +ve testing both
-----
---------------------------------------------------------------------------
| Positive Testing                    | Negative Testing                  |
| ----------------------------------- | --------------------------------- |
| Valid input                         | Invalid input                     |
| Expected success                    | Expected failure/exception        |
| Verifies normal behavior            | Verifies error handling           |
| Example: Valid login                | Example: Invalid login            |
| assertEquals(), assertNotNull()     | assertThrows(), assertFalse()     |
