Breaking down $.id

$ → means the root of the JSON object (top-level).

.id → means the property named id inside that root.

So if your response JSON looks like:

{
  "id": 10,
  "name": "Bob"
}


$.id → points to 10

$.name → points to "Bob"

More Examples:

Given this JSON:

{
  "id": 5,
  "user": {
    "name": "Alice",
    "roles": ["ADMIN", "USER"]
  }
}


$.id → 5

$.user.name → "Alice"

$.user.roles[0] → "ADMIN"

$.user.roles[1] → "USER"
